        "driver": {
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/kucherenko/jscpd/",
          "name": "jscpd",
          "rules": [
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Duplicate sections of code increase the risk of development errors, especially if fixes are made to one code block but not the other. Duplicates that share the same abstractions should be refactored into reusable helper methods as an application of the Don't Repeat Yourself principle."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kucherenko/jscpd/",
              "id": "jscpd/duplicate-code",
              "name": "jscpd/duplicate-code",
              "properties": {
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "tags": [
                  "quality"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Duplicated code detected"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Functions and methods whose normalized syntax trees share at least --similarity of their subtrees (Type-3 clones found by structure rather than by a token run). The names of the functions and methods they call and their operators count; local names, field names and literals do not, as long as each name stands for one name on the other side. The similarity property holds the Jaccard index of the two trees' subtree fingerprints, and the nodes property the size of each tree."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kucherenko/jscpd/",
              "id": "jscpd/similar-function",
              "name": "jscpd/similar-function",
              "properties": {
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "tags": [
                  "quality"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Functions with a similar structure detected"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Functions that appear to do the same thing written differently, possibly in different languages (Type-4 clones, --semantic, experimental). Found by comparing embeddings of the functions' code: each function is the other's closest match and their cosine similarity, held in the similarity property, reaches the configured threshold. Review before refactoring; an embedding model can pair functions that are related without being duplicates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kucherenko/jscpd/",
              "id": "jscpd/semantic-code",
              "name": "jscpd/semantic-code",
              "properties": {
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "tags": [
                  "quality"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Semantically similar code detected"
              }
            }
